1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,820
Good morning everyone.I’m Steve Wainwright, from Elmleigh Town Council,

2
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:08,910
and I organise the town’s volunteer scheme.

3
00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:12,700
I’m delighted you’re all interested in joining the scheme.

4
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:17,576
Our volunteers help to create a sense of community among the many people who

5
00:00:17,576 --> 00:00:19,863
live in our historic town of Elmleigh,

6
00:00:19,863 --> 00:00:25,240
and make residents and visitors feel welcome at local events.

7
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:30,980
First I’ll mention just a few of the activities that volunteers carry out.

8
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:37,090
One is to walk around the town centre streets wearing our volunteer T-shirt.

9
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:40,221
Tourists often ask how to get to a particular shop,

10
00:00:40,221 --> 00:00:45,680
and they might also be grateful for recommendations about what to visit.

11
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:48,972
The town holds a large number of concerts each year,

12
00:00:48,972 --> 00:00:53,668
and part of the volunteers’ role is to get everyone in the audience to

13
00:00:53,668 --> 00:00:57,020
the right place as smoothly as possible.

14
00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:01,800
You’d be surprised how many people buy tickets then don’t check them,

15
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:04,290
and head for the wrong section of the hall!

16
00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:12,290
Volunteers may get involved with community groups, such as sports clubs or gardeners’ associations.

17
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:17,050
Here the volunteers talk about how groups can help each other.

18
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:22,046
For instance, a writing group might want to travel to another town to hear

19
00:01:22,046 --> 00:01:23,751
a talk by a well-known author,

20
00:01:23,751 --> 00:01:29,570
but may not know that another club has a coach they could travel in.

21
00:01:29,570 --> 00:01:31,582
The town produces a monthly magazine,

22
00:01:31,582 --> 00:01:36,290
and anyone who lives in the town can send in articles.

23
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:38,136
It’s free to residents,

24
00:01:38,136 --> 00:01:45,460
and is paid for by local businesses – that’s the responsibility of the council’s

25
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:45,510
advertising department.

26
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:50,583
We depend on volunteers, though, to find out what people think of events they’ve

27
00:01:50,583 --> 00:01:51,588
attended,

28
00:01:51,588 --> 00:01:54,280
and any suggestions they have for the future.

29
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:58,490
The volunteers then send a summary to the editors.

30
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:01,664
There are a number of clubs for retired people,

31
00:02:01,664 --> 00:02:07,250
and every year, the council arranges lunch for all the members.

32
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:09,335
The volunteers welcome the guests,

33
00:02:09,335 --> 00:02:14,127
and when everyone’s sitting down and relaxing after the meal, some volunteers put on

34
00:02:14,127 --> 00:02:19,240
a show – usually around half an hour of songs and short plays.

35
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:23,461
The club members really welcome the chance to chat to the volunteers at these

36
00:02:23,461 --> 00:02:25,170
events.

37
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:27,399
The town council has a website, of course,

38
00:02:27,399 --> 00:02:32,940
and volunteers are asked to help by making sure residents know about it.

39
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:37,484
It’s updated every day with information about future activities,

40
00:02:37,484 --> 00:02:40,520
and we want as many people as possible to use it.

41
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:45,740
OK, now you know some of the things our volunteers do, I’ll go on

42
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:48,430
to some practical matters.

43
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:53,026
As you probably know, the town arranges three major festivals every year,

44
00:02:53,026 --> 00:02:57,240
and they all depend on a large number of volunteers.

45
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:59,431
The book festival lasts three days,

46
00:02:59,431 --> 00:03:01,481
and uses several venues,

47
00:03:01,481 --> 00:03:03,430
which all need volunteers.

48
00:03:03,430 --> 00:03:05,478
More are needed for the music festival,

49
00:03:05,478 --> 00:03:07,667
because that lasts a whole week,

50
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:11,965
and even more help is required for the science festival, even though it’s only

51
00:03:11,965 --> 00:03:13,170
two days long.

52
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:16,630
It involves quite a lot of venues, though.

53
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:21,248
It’s a good idea to help at the festival you’re most interested

54
00:03:21,248 --> 00:03:21,369
in,

55
00:03:21,369 --> 00:03:24,220
because you can attend most of the events for free.

56
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:27,248
We try to use volunteers who are flexible, though,

57
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:30,116
because some festival events are held outdoors,

58
00:03:30,116 --> 00:03:32,743
and the weather may affect the size of the audience,

59
00:03:32,743 --> 00:03:35,390
and even whether the event can take place;

60
00:03:35,390 --> 00:03:39,060
so there can be changes at short notice.

61
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:44,614
What’s essential, though, is being able to get on well with other people,

62
00:03:44,614 --> 00:03:50,970
and also to deal with someone who’s behaving badly – as occasionally happens.

63
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:56,664
Our plan is to get you all working in September, after a week’s training

64
00:03:56,664 --> 00:03:57,710
starting on the 2nd.

65
00:03:57,710 --> 00:04:03,170
So we’ll be timetabling you for duties the following week, from the 9th

66
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:03,220
onward.

67
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:08,283
Later, in the week beginning September 23rd, we have a chat with each of

68
00:04:08,283 --> 00:04:11,231
you, to find out how you feel about being a volunteer,

69
00:04:11,231 --> 00:04:14,740
and what extra support you need.

70
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:19,730
As a thank you to the volunteers, we arrange an annual event.

71
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:23,711
In recent years we’ve had a party in the town hall,

72
00:04:23,711 --> 00:04:27,250
and last year a barbecue in Chamber Park.

73
00:04:27,250 --> 00:04:31,664
Our forthcoming event is a trip along the canal from here to Dewhurst

74
00:04:31,664 --> 00:04:32,490
and back.

75
00:04:32,490 --> 00:04:35,649
It’s on Saturday September the 28th,

76
00:04:35,649 --> 00:04:38,905
and if you’d like to attend, you can sign up once you start

77
00:04:38,905 --> 00:04:39,210
work.

78
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:43,250
Now this is the volunteers’ T-shirt …
